title: StructureMenu
tags: structure interaction
---
// The ONE parameterized building-interaction node. The caller sets $structureId
// (DialogueService.PlayStructure); everything below is data-driven from that id —
// the portrait (Portraits/<id>), the name/level/yield, and the upgrade cost — so a
// building can only ever surface its OWN domain (no out-of-domain options).
//   Buy / Sell  = silo-scoped stubs (empty sets for now, extensible).
//   Upgrade     = the live option (levels + perks via the economy backend).
//   Talk        = narrative/questline seed (e.g. the Forge's "forgotten hammer").
<<portrait Portraits/{$structureId}>>
<<structure_status $structureId>>

{$structureName}: Need something?

-> Upgrade — {$upgradeCostText} <<if !$structureMaxed>>
    <<structure_upgrade $structureId>>
    {$structureName}: {$upgradeResult}
-> Buy
    {$structureName}: Nothing in stock just yet — come back soon.
-> Sell
    {$structureName}: I'm not buying at the moment.
-> Talk
    <<structure_talk $structureId>>
    {$structureName}: Always work to be done around here. Stick around and I might have a task for you.
-> Leave
    {$structureName}: Safe travels.
===

title: PetHouse
tags: structure interaction pet
---
// The pet house's OWN flow: "visit the pet house to name and select your pet."
// The player selects a guardian SPECIES via Yarn options; <<spawn_named_pet>>
// deploys the chosen species through the self-healed PetDeployer (DialogueCommandBridge).
// DialogueService.PlayStructure("pet-house", …) routes here (not the generic StructureMenu).
//
// TODO: free-text pet NAMING — Yarn options can't capture typed text, so the pet
// takes its catalog name for now (Aether Sprite / Flame Pup / Ice Wolf). A code-built
// name-entry UI (cf. PetIntroduction) would write GameState.PetName before deploy.
<<portrait Portraits/pet-house>>
{$structureName}: Welcome to the Pet House. Choose a guardian to stand with you — they'll fight at your side and gather while you defend.

-> A frost-warden — the Ice Wolf. Steady and tough.
    <<spawn_named_pet "ice-wolf">>
    {$structureName}: The Ice Wolf is yours. It'll chill any foe that nears the Heart.
-> A hearth-hound — the Flame Pup. Fierce and fast.
    <<spawn_named_pet "flame-pup">>
    {$structureName}: The Flame Pup answers your call. Its embers will scorch the enemy.
-> A heart-ward — the Aether Sprite. Quick and arcane.
    <<spawn_named_pet "aether-sprite">>
    {$structureName}: The Aether Sprite flits to your side. It'll ward the Heart with arcane light.
-> Not yet — I'll come back.
    {$structureName}: The pen's always open when you're ready.
===
